<title>USA: ERO Inc Q4 net climbs on sales gain.</title>
<headline>ERO Inc Q4 net climbs on sales gain.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNT PROSPECT, Ill. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>ERO Inc said Friday stronger sales and reduced dependency on licensing helped earnings increase sharply in the fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The company reported net income of $6.4 million, or $0.62 a share, in the period ended December 31, up from $4.7 million, or $0.45 a share, in 1995. Revenues climbed to $59.8 million from $48.2 million one year ago.</p>
<p>ERO markets children's leisure products through four operating subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Its shares were trading up 1-1/4 Friday afternoon at 10-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
